$ hibi --help
exit status: 0
---- standard output ----
hibi records that a statement was checked against evidence. Later it reports which statements need a new check because their text or their evidence changed, and which parts of a declared scope have no claim at all.

hibi decides nothing about whether a statement is true. You check it, hibi remembers that you did and what the text and the evidence looked like then.

Usage: hibi [OPTIONS] <command>

Commands:
  init              Create the .hibi/ store in this git repository
  claim             Record a statement, what it is about and its evidence, as checked now
  status            Report which claims need a new check and why
  mark              Record that claims were checked again and still hold
  reanchor          Replace a claim with one that has a new statement, anchors or period
  retire            Retire claims that no longer apply
  cover             List the units in the declared scopes that no claim covers
  list              List stored claims, or show one claim with its history
  triage            Rank uncovered prose by how likely it states a checkable fact (judge)
  suggest-evidence  Rank code units that may be evidence for a statement (judge)
  providers         Show the built-in file provider, sibling repositories and schemes
  schema            Print the JSON Schema of a record, an input or a command's output
  completions       Print a shell completion script
  version           Print the hibi version

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Global options:
      --root <dir>
          Use this directory as the root (the directory that contains .hibi/) instead of searching upward from the working directory

      --format <format>
          Output format. Without this option the output is JSON when standard output is not a terminal, and text when it is

          Possible values:
          - human: Text for a person
          - json:  One JSON object

      --now <timestamp>
          Use this instant as the current time, for reproducible runs. RFC 3339 with any offset, for example 2026-11-20T18:04:11Z. A fraction of a second is dropped

      --no-cache
          Do not read or write the cache database. Results are the same with and without the cache

Anchors:
  An anchor names one unit of a resource: a sentence, a heading, a function.
    file:docs/retry.md                     the whole file
    file:src/retry.rs#fetch_with_retry     the declaration with this symbol
    file:docs/retry.md::capped at 30 s     the unit that contains this quote
    file:src/retry.rs#retry::MAX = 5       a quote inside a symbol
  Use repo:<alias>//<path> for a file in a sibling repository. A path that
  contains '#' or '::', and any selector for an external scheme, is given as
  JSON on standard input (claim --stdin).

Output:
  The result is JSON when standard output is not a terminal, or with
  --format json: one object with "ok", "command" and the result keys, or
  with "ok": false and "errors". Otherwise the result is text.

Exit status:
  0 when the command ran, whatever it found. 1 on any error.

Environment:
  HIBI_BY            default for --by
  HIBI_CONFIG        path of the user config file
  HIBI_CACHE_DIR     directory of the cache database
  TYPESAFE_API_KEY   key for the judge commands (triage, suggest-evidence,
                     status --judge-order); nothing else uses the network
  HIBI_JEV_URL       address of the judge service, for tests
  NO_COLOR           turn colour off in help output
